# A spell's mana value on the stack counts X as announced (CR 202.3e, 107.3; Ashling's ruling). Turn 3: Mind Twist with
# X of 2 is a spell of mana value 3, so Ashling, Rimebound's {R}{R} for "spells with mana value 4 or greater" can't pay
# for it (CR 106.6): the Mox Jet, Mox Pearl and Island mana does, and the {R}{R} stays in the pool. Turn 5: Rimebound's two
# "at the beginning of your first main phase" abilities trigger, the {R} to transform back is declined, and Mox Ruby's {R}
# goes to Lightning Bolt. The new {R}{R} with Mox Jet and Mox Pearl then casts Shatterskull Smashing - the front face of a
# modal double-faced card, a spell of mana value 2 + X (CR 712.8f) - with X of 2. It is offered with no other red mana
# left though at X of 0 its {R}{R} (mana value 2) could not be paid with that mana: X is still to be announced (CR 601.2b).
# It deals 2 damage to Ashling, which survives.

